1:"In PayRadar, on-device records and cloud sync are separate concerns. Offline use, synchronisation and reminders each have their own boundaries, described in the product notes.",cap2Title:"Keep the route to a result visible.",cap2:"EIP centres on documents and work samples. Pharos brings source records and changes over time into view, so a match can be examined with its context.",cap3Title:"Give pending work a place.",cap3:"In Bungalow OS, reservations, maintenance and approvals are connected. The design focuses on the next task, the exception and the point where a person needs to decide.",toolbeltLabel:'BUILDING WITH',collectionLabel:"03 / THE WORK",collectionTitle:"Products, tools<br><em>and work in progress.</em>",collectionIntro:"These projects are at different stages. Accessible product pages, development projects and open-source starters are labelled accordingly.",filterAll:'All',filterPlatforms:'Platforms',filterApps:'Applications',filterIntelligence:'Research & AI',filterTools:'Tools',filterWeb:'Web & experience',search:'Find a product or technology',updated:'SOURCE REVIEW / 24.10.2026',noResults:'No work matches this search. Try another word.',showMore:'Show more work',companyLabel:'04 / VOYAGERROC TECHNOLOGIES',companyTitle:"Where does the next<br><em>developer pick up?</em>",founderRole:'Product & systems',companyLead:"For a client, that question is about continuity. For a developer, it means understanding the decisions, dependencies and work still left open.",companyBody:"That is our working standard: describe the job, then choose the tools it calls for. We use AI in research, design and code production. Scope, data access and acceptance criteria still need explicit decisions.",companyVision:"When discussing a project, we want to put the problem, the exclusions and the definition of done in writing. We present our products with the same care: what is available, what is in development and what has yet to be verified.",aiNote:"An AI-generated line is still part of the product. Understanding it, checking it where needed and being able to change it are part of our approach.",contactLabel:'05 / CONTACT',contactTitle:"Where is the work<br><em>getting stuck?</em>",contactDescription:"Tell us about the current workflow, where it stalls and the result you need. For a product enquiry, include its name so we can start with the specifics.",corporateLabel:'BUSINESS ENQUIRIES',directLabel:'DIRECT CONTACT',backTop:'Back to top ↑',methodLabel:'How should you read product statuses? +',methodClose:'Product status notes −',methodText:'Products are presented through source inspection and accessible pages. A page opening does not mean every workflow passed end-to-end testing. Prototypes, source projects and available product surfaces are labelled separately. Each project explains its current scope and limitations.',projectDetails:'PRODUCT NOTES',details:'Explore the product',workDetails:'Explore the work',problem:'THE NEED',approach:'PRODUCT APPROACH',scope:'CURRENT SCOPE',openWeb:'Open the web page',androidGuide:'Test installation guide',androidTest:'Google Play · Android test',openCode:'Explore the source',askProject:'Talk about this product',checked:'Source and scope review: 24 October 2026',close:'Close',cardCount:'projects',schematic:'SCHEMATIC PRODUCT VIEW',exampleScreen:'PRODUCT SCREEN WITH SAMPLE DATA',eipHeader:'Evidence centre',eipTitle:"What supports the application.",eip1:'Documents',eip2:'Evidence',eip3:'Applications',payTitle:'Payments.',payCaption:"Dates, amounts,\nrenewals.",opsTitle:'Operations centre',ops1:'Reservations',ops2:'Housekeeping',ops3:'Awaiting approval',navLabel:'Main navigation',filterLabel:'Product category',sceneAria:'Interactive three-dimensional structure representing the product ecosystem'
